  <p>
    Please review these Terms of Service carefully prior to utilizing the BataiBato mobile application (package: <strong>com.bataibato.app</strong>) and website. By downloading, registering, or hailing rides, you agree to be bound by these provisions.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Platform Scope and Operations</h2>
  <p>
    BataiBato operates as an online digital technology coordination platform facilitating connections between independent vehicle owners (driver partners) and commuters (riders) travelling along shared routes in Sindhuli and across Nepal. BataiBato does not own transportation fleets or operate as a direct public carrier.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Eligibility and User Accounts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Users must be at least 18 years of age or possess legal parental guidance to register.</li>
    <li>Driver partners must hold a valid, unexpired government driving license issued by the Department of Transport Management (DoTM) of Nepal, alongside official vehicle blue book registration.</li>
    <li>All profile data, emergency contacts, and vehicle information must be accurate and up to date.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Safety Standards and Conduct Rules</h2>
  <p>
    To preserve a secure and respectful community transit environment, the following rules are mandatory:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Mandatory Helmets:</strong> For all motorcycle and scooter journeys, both driver and passenger must wear certified protective helmets throughout the duration of the trip.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Substance Prohibition:</strong> Operating vehicles or boarding rides under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or intoxicating substances is strictly prohibited.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Vehicle Roadworthiness:</strong> Driver partners are responsible for routine maintenance, brake safety, tire conditions, and headlight functionality.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Zero Tolerance for Misconduct:</strong> Harassment, discrimination, aggressive conduct, or illegal activities will result in immediate permanent account termination.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Fares and Payment Settlements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All platform fares are calibrated in Nepalese Rupees (NPR).</li>
    <li>Fares are calculated upfront based on trip distance, estimated duration, and vehicle tier.</li>
    <li>Accepted payment options include eSewa, Khalti, local mobile banking, or physical cash paid directly to the driver partner upon destination arrival.</li>
    <li>Arbitrary overcharging beyond the confirmed application fare is strictly forbidden.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Ride Cancellations</h2>
  <p>
    Both commuters and drivers may cancel scheduled or active match requests under valid circumstances. However, repetitive or unjustified cancellations once a driver is en route may affect user reliability scores.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
  <p>
    The BataiBato trademarks, logos, visual layouts, mobile source code, and website publications remain the exclusive intellectual property of BataiBato. Unauthorized replication or extraction is unlawful.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Limitation of Legal Liability</h2>
  <p>
    BataiBato maintains rigorous verification standards to promote passenger security. However, to the maximum extent permitted under Nepalese law, BataiBato is not directly liable for unforeseen road conditions, natural weather interruptions, or independent third party negligence.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Governing Law and Legal Venue</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service are governed by and construed in accordance with the prevailing laws of Nepal and the Motor Vehicles and Transport Management Act. Any legal disputes shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts in Sindhuli District, Nepal.
  </p>

